    "note": "NOT IN IEDB \u2014 peptides ingested from paper supplement (Table S1B, sheet DataS1B). MAPTAC (Mono-Allelic Purification with Tagged Allele Constructs) uses biotin-acceptor peptide tag + BirA \u2192 streptavidin pulldown for mono-allelic class II profiling. One allele per sample: the construct carries a single beta chain, so a pooled multi-allele sample would assert that any of the alleles could present any of the peptides. DataS1B reports HLA-DM co-transfection (peptide editing) and no-DM (CLIP-loaded, low-affinity) as separate arms for 4 of the 10 alleles. Those arms remain separate samples here even though the ingested CSV merges their peptide sets per allele; consequently an observation cannot be assigned to either arm and its arm-level metadata stays unknown. Also includes SILAC DC cross-presentation (heavy DCs + light tumor cells \u2192 distinguish cross-presented vs endogenous peptides). Lung and spleen from healthy donors. PBMCs from healthy donors. Raw MS: MassIVE MSV000083991.\n",
